1
00:00:09,490 --> 00:00:13,870
Can't focus. My body is still puzzled about what to do.

2
00:00:09,490 --> 00:00:13,870
Shuuchuu dekitenaina mada karada ga mayotteirunda

3
00:00:13,870 --> 00:00:17,630
I'm trembling. I can't stop even if I try to control myself.

4
00:00:13,870 --> 00:00:17,630
Furueteitanja kontoroorushitatte burerunda

5
00:00:17,630 --> 00:00:21,380
Although neither sun nor moon are on my side,

6
00:00:17,630 --> 00:00:21,380
Taiyou mo tsuki mo nanmo kanzen ni kocchi muiteinaiga

7
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:22,800
"I've no choice but to try,"

8
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:22,800
Yarushikanainda

9
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:25,470
Those were the words I muttered to myself.

10
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:25,470
Iikikaseruyouni sotto tsubuyaita

11
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:31,060
The odds aren't on my side, but running way'd be gutless.

12
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:31,060
Joukyou wa waruiga tada nigedasunja konjou nainaa

13
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:35,060
Even if I can't see the future, I'll just have to win it over with courage.

14
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:35,060
Tenbou wa naiga dokyou de kuria suru shika naiya

15
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:38,560
Need to keep distance from the target as I hold myself back.

16
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:38,560
Shoudou wa osaetamama taagetto to no kankaku sagure

17
00:00:38,770 --> 00:00:41,860
All that's needed for victory is pride to win.

18
00:00:38,770 --> 00:00:41,860
Hitsuyou na mon wa katsu puraido

19
00:00:41,860 --> 00:00:44,950
Will we celebrate with the wine of victory

20
00:00:41,860 --> 00:00:44,950
Ajiwau nowa shouri no bishu ka

21
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:48,950
Or'll we end up kissing their feet in defeat?

22
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:48,950
Soretomo haiboku no kujuu ka

23
00:00:48,950 --> 00:00:52,700
There are two outcomes to everything.

24
00:00:48,950 --> 00:00:52,700
Sou subete wa futatsu ni hitotsu

25
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:56,420
I want to control destiny.

26
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:56,420
Ayatsuritai unmei no ito

27
00:00:57,830 --> 00:01:01,750
I need to seize the golden opportunity with my hands.

28
00:00:57,830 --> 00:01:01,750
Zekkou no goorudentaimu kono te de tsukame

29
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:05,840
I'll finish it up with my best poker face,

30
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:05,840
Konshin no pookaafeisu kimete shikakeruyo

31
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:10,800
And drag them into a world of illusions.

32
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:10,800
Iryuujon no sekai e hikizurikonde

33
00:01:13,180 --> 00:01:17,140
I'll find my way out of this endless pressure game,

34
00:01:13,180 --> 00:01:17,140
Saigennai puresshaageemu sururito nukete

35
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:21,150
And leap over the borderline of honor.

36
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:21,150
Eikou no boodaarain tobikoeru tameni

37
00:01:21,150 --> 00:01:25,860
How many? What'll I need to sacrifice to make it happen?

38
00:01:21,150 --> 00:01:25,860
Haumenii? Dorekurai no daishou ga iru?

39
00:01:25,860 --> 00:01:30,120
What is the one thing I don't want to let go?

40
00:01:25,860 --> 00:01:30,120
Tebanashitakunai mon wa dore?

41
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:44,530
Hey, where the hell are you taking us?

42
00:01:44,530 --> 00:01:45,610
Get in.

43
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:05,300
This is...

44
00:02:07,550 --> 00:02:09,180
Military Headquarters?!

45
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:10,680
What does this mean?!

46
00:02:11,810 --> 00:02:12,720
Hey.

47
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:15,520
You guys are filthy.

48
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:22,650
I wouldn't have dreamed the Homunculi's hideout was under Headquarters...

49
00:02:22,650 --> 00:02:27,780
So it means that the army is also associated with them, not just the Führer President.

50
00:02:29,370 --> 00:02:32,620
But I've got something good to tell you, too.

51
00:02:36,250 --> 00:02:39,080
Really?! You really found my body?!

52
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:40,210
Yeah.

53
00:02:40,210 --> 00:02:44,460
Although you told me,
"You're not my soul, so I can't come with you."

54
00:02:45,010 --> 00:02:48,010
Great, so my body still exists!

55
00:02:48,010 --> 00:02:49,720
Awesome! Awesome!

56
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:50,720
Okay!

57
00:02:53,010 --> 00:02:56,810
This just means we're one step closer to our goal.

58
00:02:58,310 --> 00:03:01,610
Hey, why do you still have that cat?

59
00:03:01,610 --> 00:03:02,940
Oh, her?

60
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:04,280
Actually, inside of me, there's...

61
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:05,940
What?!

62
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:07,650
That midget?!

63
00:03:07,650 --> 00:03:09,700
Brother! Stop being so loud!

64
00:03:09,700 --> 00:03:11,990
Hurry and put your underwear on!

65
00:03:12,530 --> 00:03:14,240
What are you guys doing?! Hurry up!

66
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:18,210
No!!!

67
00:03:19,070 --> 00:03:22,070
Struggle of the Fool

68
00:03:19,070 --> 00:03:22,070
Struggle of the Fool

69
00:03:26,050 --> 00:03:29,430
Geez, why the hell did you have to bring her?

70
00:03:29,430 --> 00:03:32,260
There was no other choice. She's injured.

71
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:32,970
Hey!

72
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:37,180
I'm leaving the rest to Wrath. Go in.

73
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:38,680
Wrath?

74
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:47,240
Wrath...

75
00:03:47,650 --> 00:03:50,450
Führer President King Bradley?!

76
00:03:53,450 --> 00:03:54,530
Colonel!

77
00:03:55,660 --> 00:03:56,830
What the hell happened?

78
00:03:56,830 --> 00:03:58,250
Quite a bit.

79
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:02,540
Sergeant Fuery was transferred to the South, Warrant Officer Falman to the North,

80
00:04:02,540 --> 00:04:04,540
and Second Lieutenant Breda to the West.

81
00:04:05,130 --> 00:04:07,920
And Lieutenant Hawkeye is going to be an assistant to the Führer President.

82
00:04:11,630 --> 00:04:13,220
What the hell...

83
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:15,560
That's no more than taking hostages.

84
00:04:17,890 --> 00:04:19,560
Have a seat.

85
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:26,570
Right now, it's just us and the Führer President in this room.

86
00:04:26,820 --> 00:04:29,190
And he only has one weapon; a sword.

87
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:33,030
Yet, he's still confident he can beat all three of us?

88
00:04:39,620 --> 00:04:40,540
Führer President!

89
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:45,960
You came to visit me in the hospital once, right?

90
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:47,800
I was completely fooled.

91
00:04:48,050 --> 00:04:52,510
"Don't meddle in things.
Think of the entire army as your enemy."

92
00:04:52,970 --> 00:04:54,800
That's what I told you.

93
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:58,970
You are all important to us.

94
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:01,680
You don't need to know about the minor details,

95
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:05,100
but behave until the time comes.

96
00:05:05,690 --> 00:05:08,070
As long as you keep that promise, we won't harm you.

97
00:05:08,070 --> 00:05:13,950
And when that time comes, what'll happen to the civilians who aren't "human sacrifices" like us?

98
00:05:14,530 --> 00:05:17,910
I just told you. You don't need to know the minor details,

99
00:05:17,910 --> 00:05:19,700
Fullmetal Alchemist.

100
00:05:21,290 --> 00:05:23,710
"Fullmetal Alchemist", eh?

101
00:05:24,710 --> 00:05:28,960
I chose to become a dog of the military in order to get my body back.

102
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:36,050
But the State Alchemist Institution itself was probably created to pick out these sacrifices.

103
00:05:36,050 --> 00:05:39,430
If I'm going to be used by you guys again on top of that...

104
00:05:42,020 --> 00:05:44,640
I quit my job as a State Alchemist!

105
00:05:45,390 --> 00:05:49,400
Your proof of being a dog is covered in blood.

106
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:54,650
Whatever you guys are planning, I'll put an end to it.

107
00:05:54,650 --> 00:05:57,200
I'll tell the other alchemists, and...

108
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:59,910
What was her name again?

109
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:03,080
Oh, that's right. Winry Rockbell.

110
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:06,500
Born in Resembool.

111
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:10,500
A childhood friend of yours
and someone who is practically family.

112
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:12,840
A skilled automail mechanic.

113
00:06:13,090 --> 00:06:17,680
She currently works at Rush Valley,
and she's loved by her customers and friends.

114
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:19,720
She's a good, obedient girl.

115
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:25,180
Lay a finger on her and see what happens! People around her, too!

116
00:06:25,890 --> 00:06:27,560
So, what are you going to do?

117
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:33,280
If you still want to quit, then I'll cut her down.

118
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:43,290
Excellent.

119
00:06:43,290 --> 00:06:44,290
Excuse me...

120
00:06:44,910 --> 00:06:47,040
We get the idea.

121
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:48,420
So, umm...

122
00:06:48,420 --> 00:06:55,550
Like before, please let us continue to search for clues
for getting our bodies back while being under surveillance.

123
00:06:55,970 --> 00:06:57,170
Please.

124
00:06:58,180 --> 00:06:59,590
Very well.

125
00:06:59,590 --> 00:07:02,180
As long as you don't interfere with our plan.

126
00:07:02,180 --> 00:07:04,220
What will you do, Colonel Mustang?

127
00:07:04,220 --> 00:07:07,310
You're not going to tell me that you plan to resign from the military too, are you?

128
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:12,980
Let's see... even if I became a dog of the military, I'd rather not become a loser.

129
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:21,490
Either way, because of my ambition, I won't be able to take off this uniform or get rid of this. For now, at least.

130
00:07:22,410 --> 00:07:23,870
Very well.

131
00:07:23,870 --> 00:07:25,490
You all may leave.

132
00:07:28,330 --> 00:07:31,420
May I ask you one thing, sir?

133
00:07:31,630 --> 00:07:33,750
What is it, Colonel?

134
00:07:33,750 --> 00:07:35,840
Are you the one who killed Hughes?

135
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:40,380
No, it was not me.

136
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:41,640
Then who?

137
00:07:41,930 --> 00:07:44,140
You said "one thing", did you not?

138
00:07:46,770 --> 00:07:48,100
Please excuse me.

139
00:07:49,190 --> 00:07:51,600
Oh. Wait a moment, Alphonse.

140
00:08:02,070 --> 00:08:03,990
U-Umm... Is there something...

141
00:08:04,370 --> 00:08:06,870
No, you may leave now.

142
00:08:13,290 --> 00:08:14,710
That was so close!

143
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:17,000
A sword just went right over my head...

144
00:08:17,880 --> 00:08:19,170
Oh yeah, Colonel.

145
00:08:19,670 --> 00:08:21,970
Money. Lend me some change.

146
00:08:21,970 --> 00:08:23,550
What's this all of a sudden?

147
00:08:24,050 --> 00:08:25,180
Don't worry about it!

148
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:27,850
Man, this is all you got?

149
00:08:27,850 --> 00:08:29,520
What are you, a thief?!

150
00:08:29,520 --> 00:08:30,600
Oh well.

151
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:31,600
Later!

152
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:32,100
H-Hey!

153
00:08:32,390 --> 00:08:33,690
Sorry, Colonel!

154
00:08:33,690 --> 00:08:35,020
We'll report everything later!

155
00:08:36,190 --> 00:08:37,730
What in the world are they up to?

156
00:08:38,480 --> 00:08:40,280
Oh no, the Lieutenant!

157
00:08:47,410 --> 00:08:48,290
Lieute-

158
00:08:50,790 --> 00:08:53,170
Is something the matter, Colonel?

159
00:08:53,170 --> 00:08:55,040
You don't look very well.

160
00:08:55,210 --> 00:09:01,170
Can you blame me for feeling sick after seeing a musclehead when I was expecting to see a woman?

161
00:09:01,510 --> 00:09:02,420
Colonel!

162
00:09:03,260 --> 00:09:04,300
Lieutenant.

163
00:09:04,300 --> 00:09:05,590
Is everything okay?

164
00:09:05,590 --> 00:09:07,300
Oh, my apologies.

165
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:10,560
Lieutenant Hawkeye, just returning from the restroom, sir.

166
00:09:11,230 --> 00:09:15,310
I accepted Major Armstrong's kindness and had him take my place for a short time.

167
00:09:16,020 --> 00:09:18,110
Thank you, Major.

168
00:09:18,110 --> 00:09:19,570
No problem at all.

169
00:09:20,150 --> 00:09:21,530
You didn't run away?

170
00:09:22,030 --> 00:09:25,780
Who's the one who told me
to never give up no matter what?

171
00:09:27,370 --> 00:09:31,790
Don't regret later that you didn't run away, Lieutenant.

172
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:33,580
Like I will after all this time...

173
00:09:37,630 --> 00:09:39,000
Hello?

174
00:09:39,590 --> 00:09:42,170
Ed? What's with the sudden call?

175
00:09:42,630 --> 00:09:44,220
Did you break your automail again?

176
00:09:44,220 --> 00:09:45,260
No!

177
00:09:45,260 --> 00:09:46,840
Hey, are you okay?

178
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:48,010
Are you doing well?

179
00:09:48,180 --> 00:09:49,930
Anything new in your life?

180
00:09:49,930 --> 00:09:52,310
You're not being stalked by anyone, are you?

181
00:09:53,640 --> 00:09:54,520
Ed...

182
00:09:54,690 --> 00:09:55,520
What is it?!

183
00:09:55,980 --> 00:09:57,020
You're being creepy.

184
00:09:58,690 --> 00:09:59,770
What did you say?!

185
00:09:59,770 --> 00:10:06,200
I mean, it's rare enough for you to call, and it turns out you're worried about me?

186
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:09,280
Geez, there's something wrong here.
I bet it's going to snow tonight or something.

187
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:11,330
Hey! Do you have any idea how much I-

188
00:10:11,330 --> 00:10:12,160
Hey, thanks.

189
00:10:13,620 --> 00:10:15,830
I'm happy you called.

190
00:10:16,830 --> 00:10:17,920
Thanks.

191
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:19,380
S-Sure.

192
00:10:19,380 --> 00:10:21,460
So you're really okay, right?

193
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:24,550
Got it. Bye.

194
00:10:27,220 --> 00:10:29,220
Good, she was fine...

195
00:10:29,220 --> 00:10:32,680
It's your excitable nature that lets people take advantage of you.

196
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:34,730
Ling!

197
00:10:34,730 --> 00:10:36,850
I told you, I'm Greed.

198
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:38,900
What the hell do you want?!

199
00:10:40,190 --> 00:10:42,190
Your buddy asked me to give you this.

200
00:10:42,190 --> 00:10:43,150
Ling did?

201
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:46,110
This is in Xing's language, huh...

202
00:10:46,110 --> 00:10:47,700
What's it say?

203
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:49,620
I don't know. Can't read it.

204
00:10:49,620 --> 00:10:52,370
He wants you to give it to the woman waiting for him.

205
00:10:52,370 --> 00:10:53,240
Lan Fa-

206
00:10:53,950 --> 00:10:57,210
You're not planning on following us and killing her, are you?

207
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:59,420
I'm not that low.

208
00:10:59,420 --> 00:11:01,710
Besides, I don't like fighting girls.

209
00:11:03,210 --> 00:11:06,630
I don't lie.

210
00:11:06,630 --> 00:11:07,970
Later. Be sure to give it to her.

211
00:11:10,510 --> 00:11:11,470
Hey, Ling!

212
00:11:12,350 --> 00:11:13,810
I'm Greed.

213
00:11:29,610 --> 00:11:31,450
Who the hell was that?

214
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:36,620
What reason did he have to start the civil war
when it would ruin this country?

215
00:11:39,790 --> 00:11:40,790
Who is it?

216
00:11:43,750 --> 00:11:45,590
Is someone up there?

217
00:11:49,550 --> 00:11:51,180
You're injured.

218
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:53,220
Could you come down?

219
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:55,680
I'd like to know what's going on outside.

220
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:59,940
It's fine; the guard won't be coming again for a while.

221
00:11:59,940 --> 00:12:03,060
I'm also a doctor. I'll tend your wounds.

222
00:12:08,940 --> 00:12:10,610
An Ishbalan, huh?

223
00:12:10,610 --> 00:12:12,110
That scar on your forehead...

224
00:12:12,780 --> 00:12:14,530
Don't tell me... You're Scar?!

225
00:12:14,530 --> 00:12:16,620
Who the hell are you?

226
00:12:16,620 --> 00:12:18,290
What are you doing here?

227
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:26,550
Oh, God!

228
00:12:28,420 --> 00:12:29,800
I'm...

229
00:12:30,010 --> 00:12:34,300
I'm also an alchemist who assisted in the Ishbal Extermination!

230
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:41,690
She'll be fine. Nothing life-threatening.

231
00:12:41,850 --> 00:12:44,440
She'll get better as long as she gets some rest.

232
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:45,810
Thank goodness.

233
00:12:45,810 --> 00:12:47,270
"Thank goodness" my ass!

234
00:12:47,730 --> 00:12:49,820
Giving me more patients by the day!

235
00:12:49,820 --> 00:12:51,570
Both my bed and sofa are occupied!

236
00:12:51,570 --> 00:12:54,320
Where the hell am I supposed to sleep, huh?!

237
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:56,530
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

238
00:12:56,530 --> 00:12:59,200
Besides, two patients in my house at once?!

239
00:12:56,830 --> 00:12:58,040
Alphonse.

240
00:12:58,040 --> 00:12:59,200
Lan Fan!

241
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:01,620
You shouldn't be up!

242
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:04,790
Is... Is the young master not with you?

243
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:08,000
I-It's fine. He's alive.

244
00:13:08,420 --> 00:13:10,510
I have a message from him.

245
00:13:18,310 --> 00:13:19,310
Lan Fan?

246
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:25,400
He says... He says he's obtained a philosopher's stone...

247
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:27,940
With this, our clan is...

248
00:13:29,070 --> 00:13:34,280
That's right! I must return to my country immediately and tell my people!

249
00:13:34,570 --> 00:13:36,990
Where is he? Where is the young master?

250
00:13:38,830 --> 00:13:41,200
What? Why won't you speak?

251
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:43,580
Don't tell me something happened to him!

252
00:13:43,750 --> 00:13:45,460
Answer me, Alphonse!

253
00:13:45,460 --> 00:13:46,830
Where is the young master?!

254
00:13:51,170 --> 00:13:54,300
How is your body feeling, Greed?

255
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:56,220
So you're Wrath.

256
00:13:56,220 --> 00:13:57,550
I'm feeling fine.

257
00:13:57,550 --> 00:14:01,640
Did you hear? This body belongs to a prince of Xing.

258
00:14:01,930 --> 00:14:07,100
He wanted power that would help him become Emperor, and thus accepted me.

259
00:14:07,100 --> 00:14:08,770
He's a really interesting guy.

260
00:14:09,980 --> 00:14:15,400
Him and I once had a discussion on what it means to be a true king.

261
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:21,410
He said something like, "A King exists for his people. Without his people, there is no King."

262
